# `scripts/verify-mainnet-guard.mjs`'s on-disk sidecar. It exists for the ~2 seconds that script
# holds `packages/protocol/src/constants.ts` flipped to sepolia, and it is the ONLY layer that
# survives a SIGKILL — the next run finds it, restores from it, and says so. If you are reading
# this because the file is sitting in your tree, a previous verify run was killed mid-flip: just
# run `npm run verify:mainnet-guard` again and it will heal itself before doing anything else.
#
# The glob also covers `.lock` (the pid of a live run, so two runs cannot flip the file underneath
# each other) and `.displaced` (the copy the self-heal set aside rather than silently overwrite).
.guard-verify-backup*

# The relayer's durable sponsorship ledger. Runtime state of one deployment, and it holds
# the salt that keys its hashed visitor ids — see packages/relayer/src/sponsorship-store.ts.
.relayer/

# Cairo / Scarb build output. Scarb.lock IS committed; target/ is not.
contracts/target/
contracts/.snfoundry_cache/

# Research and competitive analysis — not for the public repo
context/
rfps.md
# `docs/*` rather than `docs/`, so a single file can be un-excluded below. Git does not
# descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a negation under a plain `docs/` would never fire.
docs/*
# The operator-facing deployment topology (story 1.6 / AD-17). It SHIPS: it is the doc that
# gives every process a named host, every relayer job its degrade state, and the cold-start
# caveat somewhere an operator or a reviewer will actually meet it — which is the whole point
# of writing it. It is neither research nor competitive analysis, so the rule above does not
# describe it. Everything else under docs/ (the retired Superpowers plans) stays excluded.
!docs/topology.md
# The user-facing privacy page (story 6.7 / FR-058). It SHIPS for the same reason, and it has a
# second reason topology does not: `scripts/build-web.mjs` READS IT and fails the build when it
# disagrees with `packages/protocol/src/visibility-matrix.ts`. Left excluded, a fresh clone has no
# such file and the build dies on ENOENT inside a gate, which is the least legible failure in the
# repository. Regenerate with `pnpm run render:privacy` and commit the result.
!docs/privacy.md

# Upstream sources cloned for ground truth — not ours to ship
reference/
